work,  there  are  three phases of interaction between client and
server: The system firmware loads a boot program.  The boot  pro‐
gram  loads  a  kernel.  The kernel performs an mount of the root
file system.  Each of these phases are described in  further  de‐
tail  below.   In  phase 1, the system firmware loads a boot pro‐
gram.  Firmware designs vary widely, so this phase is  inherently
machine‐specific.   Some examples: Alpha systems use to determine
